  "title": "Major Bank Digital Transition Map",
  "question": "Where is each major incumbent in the transition from research and roadmap to live money, assets, custody, settlement, collateral and publicly demonstrated recovery, including the quiet migration of retirement fund records and operating rails beneath conventional participant interfaces?",
  "bluf": "Sixteen major incumbents are not converging on one bank-on-blockchain model. Fidelity adds a national-trust-bank digital custodian, the live FIDD stablecoin, a bounded FYOXX OnChain fund-share record, collateral accounts and a plan-sponsor-gated workplace retirement route. Its retirement reach is distribution leverage, not universal authority over plan menus or assets. The quiet retirement transition can occur beneath an unchanged participant interface: fund-share DLT, the plan trust's holding, the participant-benefit record and contribution or settlement cash are separate layers. Live Fidelity and Franklin fund-record models do not yet establish a tokenized U.S. workplace target-date fund or CIT, plan-level DLT record, or digital-cash benefit rail. No institution proves recurring scale plus public stress, correction, recovery and legacy retirement across all seven surfaces.",
